  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14249971/assets/731237ee8d4ea5fdb53c50971bad11dd9f4317f595ae9af95846b17b6d064fce.png)\n\nThe function $g(x)$ is defined and differentiable on $[-5,3].$ The graph of ${g}^{′}(x),$ the derivative of $g(x),$ is shown above, where the area of the region between the graph and the $x$-axis is $7.$\n\nGiven that $g(3)=4,$ what is the minimum value ${g}_{\\text{min}}$ of $g(x)$ on the interval $[-5,3]?$\n\n${g}_{\\text{min}}=$\n{{field-1}}",
